The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
aiu->i2s.irq = platform_get_irq_byname(pdev, "i2s");
aiu->spdif.irq = platform_get_irq_byname(pdev, "spdif");
```
Reason:
The IRQ values returned by `platform_get_irq_byname()` can be negative in case of an error (e.g., if the IRQ is not found). Storing these values in an unsigned integer type (`aiu->i2s.irq` and `aiu->spdif.irq`) can lead to the loss of this negative error code, resulting in incorrect error handling and potential undefined behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (aiu->i2s.irq < 0)
    return aiu->i2s.irq;
if (aiu->spdif.irq < 0)
    return aiu->spdif.irq;
```
Reason:
These statements check if the IRQ values are negative and return the error code if they are. This ensures that any error during IRQ registration is properly handled, allowing the function to exit gracefully with the correct error code instead of misrepresenting it due to the unsigned integer type.

